          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.2 HOW DO OUR ACTIVITIES AFFECT THE ENVIRONMENT?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.657,
            0.901,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are an integral part of the environment. Changes in the environment affect us and our activities change the environment around us. We have already seen in Class IX how our activities pollute the environment. In this chapter, we shall be looking at two of the environmental problems in detail, that is, depletion of the ozone layer and waste disposal.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.762,
            0.832,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.2.1 Ozone Layer and How it is Getting Depleted"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.793,
            0.901,
            0.874
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ozone "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\mathrm { O } _ { 3 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a molecule formed by three atoms of oxygen. While "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { O } _ { 2 ^ { \\prime } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which we normally refer to as oxygen, is essential for all aerobic forms of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "life. Ozone, is a deadly poison. However, at the higher levels of the atmosphere, ozone performs an essential function. It shields the surface of the earth from ultraviolet (UV) radiation from the Sun. This radiation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
